    "result_text": "The full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test, 0 failures). `AcceptanceTest` is the only test class in the project.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the membership-level tenure rule in the `OwnerMapper` (the mapper is where all derived owner fields are computed).\n\n**`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 `membershipLevel(Owner)`\n- The pre-tenure factors (base 1, +1 for email present, +1 for `namesakeCount == 0`) are still capped at 3.\n- Added a level-4 bump: `+1` when tenure is more than 365 days, giving an overall max of 4.\n- Added a `tenureDays(Owner)` helper computing whole days from `registrationDate` to `LocalDate.now()` (via `ChronoUnit.DAYS.between`). A missing `registrationDate` and a today-registered owner both yield zero tenure \u2014 matching how the existing `ageBand` uses `registrationDate` as its reference point.\n\nBecause a newly created owner registers today, its tenure is 0, so it can never reach level 4 \u2014 a new owner with an email and `namesakeCount 0` lands at exactly level 3 (household size is not a factor, consistent with the test's own note).\n\n**`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 bumped the generated `OwnerDto.membershipLevel` constraint from `maximum: 3` to `maximum: 4` (level 4 is now producible) and updated its description. Without this, the generated DTO would cap/validate the field at 3.\n\nThe pre-existing acceptance test `coreNewOwnerCappedAtLevel3()` \u2014 which asserts `membershipLevel == 3` for a new owner with an email \u2014 passes.",
